Question: What is PaperQA2?

PaperQA2 is a frontier language model agent optimized for factuality in scientific research tasks (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 1-3). It is a retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) system designed to synthesize scientific knowledge from academic literature (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 17-19).

The system decomposes RAG into multiple specialized tools: a "Paper Search" tool that transforms user queries into keyword searches, a "Gather Evidence" tool that ranks paper chunks using dense vector retrieval followed by LLM reranking and contextual summarization (RCS), a "Generate Answer" tool that produces final responses, and a "Citation Traversal" tool that exploits citation graphs for hierarchical indexing (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 3-5). PaperQA2 parses papers using Grobid and stores contextual summaries in agent state (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 3-5).

On the LitQA2 benchmark, PaperQA2 achieved 85.2% precision and 66.0% accuracy, outperforming other RAG systems and achieving superhuman precision compared to human PhD-level annotators (73.8%) (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 3-5). The system demonstrates superhuman performance on three realistic literature research tasks: information retrieval from scientific literature, summarization of scientific topics into cited Wikipedia-style articles, and contradiction detection within scientific papers (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 1-3). It can identify contradictions in biology papers at scale with 70% validation by human experts (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 1-3).

